---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Getupp"
  description="Getupp privacy policy. How we handle your data, your photos, and your email."
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-neutral-500">Effective date: 9 July 2026</p>

  <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-neutral-600">
    We're two founders who are also users of this app. We built Getupp
    because we wanted it, not to build an ad network. This policy is written
    to be readable by humans, not only lawyers. If something is unclear,
    email us: <a href="mailto:hello@getupp.co">hello@getupp.co</a>.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <section aria-labelledby="pp-what">
    <h2 id="pp-what">1. What Getupp does</h2>
    <p>
      Getupp is an iOS app that uses Apple's Screen Time and Family Controls
      technology to temporarily block the apps you choose during a morning
      window you define. Each morning, those apps remain blocked until you
      take a live photo confirming you are out of bed. Once the photo is
      verified, your apps are unlocked for the day.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app is a digital wellbeing tool. It is not a parental-control
      product; it is designed for adults who want to change their own
      morning habits. You are always in control of which apps are blocked
      and during which time window.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section aria-labelledby="pp-screentime">
    <h2 id="pp-screentime">2. Screen Time &amp; app-blocking data</h2>
    <p>
      Getupp uses Apple's Family Controls framework to apply and remove app
      restrictions. All Screen Time data — including which apps are blocked
      and for how long — is processed entirely on your device. This data
      never leaves your phone and is never sent to our servers.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not collect, store, sell, or share any Screen Time or
      app-usage information. Apple's framework enforces this at the OS
      level.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>We cannot see which apps you block.</li>
      <li>We cannot see your app-usage history.</li>
      <li>
        We cannot access Screen Time data outside the scope of your session
        on your device.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section aria-labelledby="pp-photos">
    <h2 id="pp-photos">3. Your verification photo</h2>
    <p>
      Each morning, Getupp asks you to take a live photo to confirm you are
      out of bed. Here is exactly what happens to that photo:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Your photo is sent over an encrypted connection (HTTPS/TLS) to our
        AI verification service, which is powered by Anthropic's API.
      </li>
      <li>
        The AI analyzes the photo solely to determine whether you appear to
        be out of bed.
      </li>
      <li>The photo is deleted immediately after analysis. We never store it.</li>
      <li>No human at Getupp ever sees your photo.</li>
      <li>
        We keep only the result (pass or fail), the timestamp, and your
        streak count.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-4 text-sm">
      <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">About Anthropic</strong>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Anthropic acts as a data processor on our behalf for photo
        verification. Anthropic does not use data sent via their API to
        train their models. For Anthropic's current API data usage policy,
        visit
        <!-- TODO: founder to re-verify Anthropic's current API data policy URL and confirm this statement before publishing -->
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >anthropic.com/privacy</a
        >.
      </p>
      <!-- TODO: founder to re-verify Anthropic's current API data policy before publishing. -->
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section aria-labelledby="pp-account">
    <h2 id="pp-account">4. Account &amp; email</h2>
    <p>
      If you join our waitlist, we collect your email address. We use it
      only to notify you when Getupp is available on the App Store and to
      send occasional pre-launch updates. We do not sell your email
      address. We do not share it with third parties for marketing
      purposes.
    </p>
    <!-- TODO: Confirm unsubscribe mechanism before launch (link in email, or in-app) -->
    <p>
      You can unsubscribe from waitlist emails at any time using the
      unsubscribe link in any email we send. After launch, account deletion
      will remove your email and all associated data from our servers.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use Supabase to store waitlist emails. Supabase is a US-based
      cloud infrastructure provider. For more information, see
      <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >supabase.com/privacy</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section aria-labelledby="pp-dont">
    <h2 id="pp-dont">5. Data we do not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not sell your data. Ever.</li>
      <li>We do not serve ads.</li>
      <li>
        We do not share personal data with third parties except as
        described above (Anthropic for photo verification; Supabase for
        email storage).
      </li>
      <li>We do not use tracking pixels or third-party analytics SDKs in the app.</li>
      <li>
        We do not access your contacts, location, microphone, or camera
        roll — only the live photo you explicitly take within the app.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section aria-labelledby="pp-children">
    <h2 id="pp-children">6. Children</h2>
    <p>
      Getupp is intended for users aged 17 and over and is not directed at
      children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information
      from anyone under 13. If you believe a child has submitted
      information to us, please contact us and we will delete it promptly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section aria-labelledby="pp-changes">
    <h2 id="pp-changes">7. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we make material changes to this policy, we will notify waitlist
      subscribers by email and update the effective date above. Continued
      use of the app after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated
      policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section aria-labelledby="pp-contact">
    <h2 id="pp-contact">8. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions, requests, or concerns about your data:<br />
      <a href="mailto:hello@getupp.co">hello@getupp.co</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Mailing address:</strong><br />
      Getupp<br />
      hello@getupp.co
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
